course: dictionary
lesson: 12222
title: Conscript: made to join by law
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A conscript is a person who is made, by law, to join the army or other armed forces. To conscript someone means to make them join the armed forces by law. They do not get to choose.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The government decided to conscript all men of a certain age.» The words decided, law and army tell you this is about forcing people to serve. Try your meaning in the sentence: "decided to make all men of a certain age join the army by law" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Conscript can be a noun (a person) or a verb (an action). «He was a conscript and had to leave his job to join the army.» Here it is a person. «The country may conscript young people next year.» Here it is an action. The noun conscription means the system of making people join by law.
fact: A conscript (noun) is a person who is made by law to join the army or armed forces.
fact: To conscript (verb) means to make someone join the armed forces by law.
fact: Conscription is the system of making people join the armed forces by law.
fact: Many young men were conscripted in both World Wars.
fact: Some countries still conscript young people today, including Ukraine during the war.
exercise: «Many young men were conscripted into the army in both World Wars.» What does conscripted mean? | Chose to join the army for fun | Paid a lot of money to be a soldier | *Made to join the armed forces by law | Sent home from the army early
exercise: «He was a conscript and had to leave his job to join the army.» What is a conscript? | A person who volunteers because they want to | A person who sells food to soldiers | A person who wrote the army's rules | *A person made by law to join the armed forces
exercise: Which sentence uses conscript as a verb, meaning to make someone join by law? | *The government may conscript young people next year. | The conscript was tall and strong. | Conscription is the system of making people join by law.
test: What does conscription mean? | A cheap price for an army uniform | *The system of making people join the armed forces by law | A group of soldiers who volunteer | Sitting an exam about the army
test: Which word means to make someone join the armed forces by law? | retire | discharge | volunteer | *conscript
exam: Jayden asks: Is a conscript someone who chose to join the army? | No, a conscript is a teacher who trains soldiers | *No, a conscript is made to join by law, so they have no choice | Yes, conscripts always volunteer | Yes, but only in peacetime
